// THE SMALLEST FAILING CASE, if the bisect is right: TWO modules, whose `parse_ask`
// differ in SIGNATURE, and neither is imported by name.
//
// The four runs that led here, each one difference from the last:
//   main.nv           2 modules, same signature, imported by name  -> built
//   main_three.nv     3 modules, one overload,   imported by name  -> built
//   main_internal3.nv 3 modules, same signature, internal          -> built
//   main_internal.nv  3 modules, one overload,   internal          -> FAILED
//
// So both are needed: an overload AND no by-name import. This asks whether two
// modules suffice once both hold.

module probe_fn_symbol_loses_module_1097.main_minimal

